gobject-introspection's scanner on Windows, for GTK's SDK (llvm-mingw's
Clang outside MSYS2, builds on a subst drive):

- a CC that isn't cl or clang-cl is GCC-like (mingw32), not distutils'
  default, msvc (MSYS2 builds say so with MSYSTEM);
- libraries are looked for where pkg-config says too, as the compiler
  doesn't search the SDK's lib by itself;
- the lexer resolves a file name as Python's os.path.realpath does the
  scanner's list of files (GetFinalPathNameByHandle), not with
  GetFullPathName alone: on a subst drive, a header the preprocessor
  names relatively wasn't one of the scanned files, and what it declares
  (a library's generated enum types) was left out.

--- a/giscanner/ccompiler.py
+++ b/giscanner/ccompiler.py
